import orchestrate as team
team.JOBS={
 'settings': '''Create ONLY dist/settings.js, ES module export createSettings({onChange,onResume,onPause}={}) -> {get values(),open(),close(),destroy()}. Original nautical pause/settings UI for a first-person cooperative raft game. Inject a <dialog id="options"> and its own CSS only if not present; visually navy translucent panels, warm bronze edges, cream labels and amber selected controls, no emoji. Heading 'Paused', Resume button, options controls with actual labels and displayed values: mouse sensitivity slider .4..2 default1; field of view60..95 default75; camera motion0..1 default.35; sound volume0..1 default.5; graphics select low/medium/high defaultmedium. Persist validated options under localStorage little-raft-settings. values returns COPY. onChange(newValues) runs on real changes and once creation. Escape key: if game active (body.playing or body.first-person), opens dialog and releases pointer lock; if open closes and calls onResume; do not open if another dialog already open (let existing Escape close it). Pointer lock may auto release before Escape key event; still open settings. Focus loss of pointerlock alone should not open pause for intentional menus. Use keydown capture, prevent repeat, event.preventDefault only when handling; Escape native dialog cancel must preventDefault and close via our callback to resume. Open invokes onPause, document.exitPointerLock if active. close invokes onResume which engine uses to request lock; don't lock pointer directly automatically. Resume actual click is user gesture. Add buttons How to play (open existing #help dialog after close without resume?) and Play together (#crew existing) if useful but no reload/reset/quit buttons needed. Add visible fullscreen toggle button using document.documentElement.requestFullscreen, label flips. Use dialog click and form inputs, all APIs normal no external assets. Error on localStorage silently defaults. destroy aborts own listeners, closes/removes only OWN dialog/style; old engine dispose may be called AFTER new settings mounted, so ownership token needed to avoid removing the new worker's dialog or style; simplest reuse existing dialog but each instance tracks own handlers, destroy aborts only and leave stable nodes in DOM. On hot creation preserve open state/slider values and don't overwrite a currently focused control. This module will be imported by synchronous engine.mount; no auto actions on import. NO shell, git, deployment, dependencies or more agents. Return API and integration details.''',
 'hand-animation': '''Create ONLY dist/hands.js export createHands(T, hookModel) -> {group,handTip,tool,update(params),dispose()}. This is original first-person Raft-style hand animation, no copied assets. User wants convincing visible pullback/throw/reeling animation. group attaches directly to perspective camera at origin, FOV75, looking -Z. Right bare hand grips supplied hookModel at about (.38,-.32,-.8); model from createHook(T) centered size .72x.84x.38 must be scaled .5 or .6. Model has handle bottom; right hand should align to lower handle, not float. Include more detailed human hands/forearms skin warm tan, fingers/thumb as simple tapered/capsule meshes, a few knuckle creases, sleeve cuffs, left hand and coiled rope. Keep <=45 total own meshes, no textures/external files, no scene/timers. Both hands should frame bottom-right/bottom-left without blocking crosshair. handTip is Object3D rope anchor at left hand/coil, use getWorldPosition after update. tool references supplied hookModel for visibility/pose. update({dt,time,charge=0,reeling=false,casting=0,walking=false,hasHookOut=false,motion=.35}) does: idle slow breathing and restrained walk sway; charging pulls RIGHT hand/tool backward down/right progressively, rotates wrist, LEFT hand holds rope; casting 0..1 impulse supplied normalized remaining pulse (1 newly released) sweeps arm forward then settles; reeling shows alternating pulling left hand rhythm and small right wrist stabilization, rope spool rotates; hasHookOut hides tool but hands/rope stay, when returns reappears. All frame-rate independent from absolute time/charge and easing; avoid cumulative transform drift. No cursor or DOM. No global light changes. Materials MeshStandardMaterial, metal only supplied model, no cast shadows for viewmodel, frustumCulled=false. root.userData orientation comments. dispose own geometries/materials only, not supplied model (engine scene handles). Return pose offsets and integration example. Do not edit game.js or other files, no shell/git/deploy/further agents.''',
 'craft-models': '''Create ONLY dist/crafts.js export createCraft(T,type) -> THREE.Group or null for unrecognized. Detailed readable original raft craft models for a first-person cooperative browser game, user wants more realistic designs resembling nautical Raft reference: worn timber, tied rope, cream canvas, steel fittings. Five types sail,palm,lantern,net plus OPTIONAL bench,crate (only if easy). Group position base is center of 2x2 raft floor at y=.22; assets should fit ~1.7x1.7 foot print, heights sail3.7 palm2.3 lantern1.9 net .2. Build sail with real bowed cloth using subdivided PlaneGeometry adjusted vertex z, mast, cross spars, ropes made TubeGeometry straight/curved, seam strips/stitches modest count, triangular pennant. Palm pot terracotta rim/soil, curved trunk segments, believable flattened pointed fronds made custom BufferGeometry or curved strips, no cones that look like spikes. Lantern wood post with crook arm, hanging metal framed amber lantern/cap/glass translucent MeshStandardMaterial, warm emissive light core but NO actual PointLight (many crafted lamps shouldn't add dozens drawlights). Net framed square timber, sagging rope lattice using TubeGeometry, floats corners, center visible empty holes, actual automatic gathering managed elsewhere. Bench/crate if present warm timber slats, joins, nails. Max ~55 meshes/type ideally less, share local geometries and materials within model, no textures/no imports/no dependencies/no scene/timers. Every mesh except glass castShadow true receiveShadow true. Each owns geometries independent from other craft instances because raft rebuild disposes all. User youngest six so recognizable shapes and clear silhouettes, detailed not photorealistic assets. No emojis, copied game assets, UI edits. Only crafts.js, no shell/git/deploy or further agents. Return types/dimensions details.'''
}
team.launch()
